  "cards": [
    {"dot": "cyan", "title": "Identity precedes analysis", "items": ["Bindings contain RunID, source SHA-256 and manifest SHA-256. A finished capture must have a matching audit-ready marker (internal/analyst/occurrence.go:33-90).", "Catalogue searches include 1-8 authorized captures and explicit record types. The first capture is the novelty target; later captures form its baseline (docs/evidence.md:178-195).", "Source selection never silently changes to a different capture (analyst_handlers.go:56-67)."]},
    {"dot": "amber", "title": "A match stays attached to exact bytes", "items": ["Occurrence references bind file/frame hashes, type, ordinal, timestamp and capture identity (internal/analyst/occurrence.go:39-48).", "Changed evidence fails resolution with HTTP 409. Later catalogue pages require the first page's snapshot hash (analyst_handlers.go:30-34,140; docs/evidence.md:193).", "The arrows show call order, not measured latency. Coverage limits and missing fields qualify novelty; they do not prove global absence (docs/evidence.md:189-193)."]},
    {"dot": "emerald", "title": "Review is an explicit state change", "items": ["Documents are saved with revision CAS, a private lock and atomic replacement (internal/analyst/workspace.go:69-194).", "A reviewer is required. Changed content must be saved as a draft before it can be reviewed again (workspace.go:118,151-176).", "Packet carving, child reanalysis and reviewed diagnostics are adjacent workflows; they preserve the same capture identity contracts (docs/evidence.md:49-172)."]}
  ]
